"persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198273958254/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 4, "playtime_forever": 1204, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 466, "last_played": 1731880108, "avatar": "fef49e7fa7e1997310d705b2a6158ff8dc1cdfeb"}, "language": "english", "review": "good", "timestamp_created": 1644946230, "timestamp_updated": 1644946230, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.454545468091964722", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1634050800", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 19, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "110296821", "author": {"steamid": "76561198080027308", "personaname": "M3taslvt", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/BewmBeatz/", "num_games_owned": 462, "num_reviews": 129, "playtime_forever": 1069, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 896, "last_played": 1719202128, "avatar": "7d76158ba54778b8754a1b06b4e7f6d3a2823639"}, "language": "english", "review": "You can't make a game a spiritual successor to anything if it doesn't have any spirit.\n\nThey didn't push any new ground hard enough. Turtle Rock tried with the card system and it can change the gameplay a little, but doesn't do enough to justify the many steps backward this game takes in comparison to it's \"spiritual\" predecessors. \n\nCompared to it's competition, B4B fails to deliver content-wise, gameplay-wise, and especially in atmosphere. I don't care about the characters or anything that is happening in the story, and no effort was put towards the story anyway since any character can be in any level and there isn't much of a scripted story (Which can be fine for a horde shooter IF it's fun). Nothing the game does in shooting, movement, or general gameplay feels particularly innovative. I finished the game in 15 hours, but feel no desire to replay it. Coop is ok, but the pvp is pretty stale and underwhelming compared to L4D versus. \n\nWhen I say the gameplay feels bland, It's hard to draw specifics cause it really does just play like every other generic FPS ever made. There's nothing done particularly [i]wrong[/i], but I don't think [insert generic lifeless FPS game here] is what most people want to run out and drop $60 on. \n\nInstead of Back 4 Blood, this game should have been Back in Development.", "timestamp_created": 1644936685, "timestamp_updated": 1644936685, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 6, "votes_funny": 2, "weighted_vote_score": "0.497929155826568604", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1634050800", "reactions": []}]}